{number: 136}
{title: Years I Was Caught in Sin’s Dread Snare}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Years I was caught in sin’s dread snare,
Straying far from the fold of God.
For getting His grace who died  for me,
In vanity proudly free.
Oh open my heart today,
Abide in my heart to stay,
Oh Lord come in, be my friend and my guide,
Forever more to abide
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
By thy great mercy I was saved
From my sins and from death set free
Thou camest to earth from sin to call,
to save whetched ones like me
Oh open my heart today,
Abide in my heart to stay,
Oh Lord come in, be my friend and my guide,
Fo ever more to abide
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Lord, thou did suffer much for me,
Purple robem and a crown of thorn
Thou camest to earth from sin to call,
To save wretched ones like me
Oh open my heart today,
Abide in my heart to stay,
Oh Lord come in, be my friend and my guide,
Forever more to abide
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Oh, that my foolish heart might know
Your great mercy and matches less grace
How wandering souls are saved from death
and praise your name face to face
Oh open my heart today,
Abide in my heart to stay,
Oh Lord come in, be my friend and my guide,
Forever more to abide
{end_of_verse}
